{"url":"https://openlibrary.org/api/books?bibkeys=OLID:OL27189165M,OLID:OL32131452M,OLID:OL32131453M,OLID:OL33231183M&jscmd=details&format=json","file":"data/metadata1000_261025/raw/library-e80294da2b7ac6d0.json","retrieved":"2026-10-25T14:41:00.331Z","status":200,"data":{"OLID:OL27189165M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL27189165M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27189165M/The_outsider","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/outsidermylifein0000fors_q9i4","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14656575-S.jpg","details":{"subtitle":"my life in intrigue","description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"From Frederick Forsyth, the grand master of international suspense, comes his most intriguing story ever--his own\"--\n\nHe was the RAF's youngest pilot at the age of nineteen, barely escaped the wrath of an arms dealer in Hamburg, got strafed by a MiG during the Nigerian civil war; the Stasi arrested him, the Israelis feted him, the IRA threatened him. And that's just for starters. Forsyth has been writing extraordinary real-world novels of intrigue for over forty years-- but what most people don't know is that some of his greatest stories of intrigue have been in his own life."},"links":[{"url":"9780399176074.jpg","title":"Cover image"}],"isbn_10":["0399176071"],"subject_times":["20th century"],"full_title":"The outsider my life in intrigue","lc_classifications":["PR6056.O699 Z46 2015","PR6056.O699Z46 2015"],"key":"/books/OL27189165M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL20994A","name":"Frederick Forsyth"}],"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"title":"Whispered words","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"title":"A large jar of talc","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"title":"A little boy's dream","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"title":"Learning French","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"title":"Learning German","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"title":"Back to Germany","type":{"key":"/type/t