"Biography"],"isbn_13":["9780399176074"],"pagination":"xviii, 332 pages, 16 unnumbered pages of plates","source_records":["marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run05.mrc:213840970:5257","ia:outsidermylifein0000fors_q9i4","amazon:0399176071","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2020-12-22","bwb:9780399176074","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-024.mrc:72740550:3569"],"title":"The outsider","lccn":["2015015842"],"number_of_pages":332,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"dewey_decimal_class":["823/.914"],"local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223116440513","urn:sfpl:31223116440505","urn:sfpl:31223116440646","urn:sfpl:31223116440786","urn:sfpl:31223116440760","urn:sfpl:31223116440612","urn:sfpl:31223116440497","urn:sfpl:31223116440554","urn:bwbsku:O7-BKR-091"],"subject_people":["Frederick Forsyth (1938-)"],"publish_country":"nyu","publish_date":"2015","by_statement":"Frederick Forsyth","oclc_numbers":["910621916"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL20009082W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"covers":[14656575,10993501],"ocaid":"outsidermylifein0000fors_q9i4","latest_revision":9,"revision":9,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-07-19T04:50:37.768703"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-06-11T00:59:10.548399"}}},"OLID:OL32131452M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL32131452M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL32131452M/The_outsider","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/outsidermylifein0000fors","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10794004-S.jpg","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"publish_date":"2015","publish_country":"enk","languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL20994A","name":"Frederick Forsyth"}],"oclc_numbers":["920836053"],"dewey_decimal_class":["823.914"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Federick Forsyth has seen it all. And yet he lived to tell the tale. 'We all make mistakes, but starting the Third World War would have been a rather large one. To this day, I still maintain it was not entirely my fault. But I'm getting ahead of myself. During the course of my life, I've barely escaped the wrath of an arms dealer in Hamburg, been strafed by a MiG during the Nigerian civil war, and landed during a bloody coup in Guinea-Bissau. The Stasi arrested me, the Israelis regaled me, the IRA prompted a quick move from Ireland to England, and a certain attractive Czech secret police agent - well, her actions were a bit more intimate. And that's just for starters. All of that I saw from the inside. But all that time I was, nonetheless, an outsider.' Trained first as a pilot, then as a journalist, Frederick Forsyth finally turned to fiction and became one of the most lauded thriller writers of our time. As exciting as his novels, Forsyth's autobiography is a candid look at an extraordinary life lived to the full, a life whose unique experiences have provided rich inspiration for thirteen internationally bestselling thrillers."},"subject_places":["Great Britain"],"subject_people":["Frederick Forsyth (1938-)"],"subjects":["English Novelists","Biography","Journalists"],"subject_times":["20th century"],"title":"The outsider","subtitle":"my life in intrigue","by_statement":"Frederick Forsyth","publishers":["Bantam Press"],"publish_places":["London"],"isbn_13":["9780593075401","9780593075418","9781473525863"],"isbn_10":["0593075404"],"pagination":"1 volume","ocaid":"outsidermylifein0000fors","source_records":["ia:outsidermylifein0000fors","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2020-11-19"],"full_title":"The outsider my life in intrigue","covers":[10794004],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL20009082W"}],"key":"/books/OL32131452M","local_id":["urn:bwbsku:KO-157-320"],"latest_revision":4,"revision":4,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-03-27T18:34:41.211698"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-06-11T00:59:10.548399"}}},"OLID:OL32131453M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL32131453M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/book